  "id": "stitchnbitch",
  "neon": "#6affa8",
  "note": "STITCH 'N' BITCH — the walk-in clinic on Ironside Street, the twin of Co-Pay & Pray.\n\nThe tile's prose: a walk-in clinic behind reinforced glass, a green cross guttering above the\ndoor, and a queue that started before dawn. Co-Pay & Pray keeps the `clinic` arm; this one is\nsmaller and busier, and the difference is the queue. A rail of bollards runs along the kerb.\n\nThe front is three bays: a pale entrance porch in the middle with a hood over the door, and a\nwindow of wired glass either side of it, lit dull green from inside. Pale piers frame the bays\nunder a parapet band that carries the name. The cross stands on the parapet over the door at a\nthird of its brightness, because it is guttering. The trade word goes on a hanzi blade at the\ncorner, a second sign that says `$trade` rather than repeating the name.\n\nThe pale trim is `ty_ff_white` render. `ty_clinic` is in the window-grid family and would paint\na second set of windows on the porch and the parapet band.\n\nIt stands in for the `stitch` arm (`replaces`), which stays in LEGACY_MODELS and comes back\nwith RENDER_TUNE.legacyArms.",
  "pal": "ty_stitch",
  "replaces": "stitch",
